 "observations": [
  "The page number «161» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it, the rule broken near its left end; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 50», in bold sans serif, underlined. At the foot, the signature line of the printed sheet: «D. K. D. Vidensk. Selsk. Skr., 7. Række, hist. og filos. Afd. III. 1.» on the left and the sheet number «21» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line. The titles (L01-L04), in bold, the sigla in roman: N's title, O's «Tadil elzohara», C's «Examinatio Veneris»; L04, «Locus autem draconis eius 1. 29. 27», in smaller bold type, followed by «(CN)». The folios of the manuscripts stand at the right of L03 and L04, «C 67v, O 125r,» and «N 32r.», the letters raised; here as right margin notes.",
  "The table: rules and heads as on p. 160 (JP2 0192), with «Pagina numerorum (O) Semita numeri (C)» over the four columns of the arguments, divided below a rule into «Augmentum proprietatum omnium1)» and «Diminutio proprietatum omnium2)» in smaller type; «Sublimatio ascensus3) Veneris examinata4)»; «Examinatio ipsius elheza5)» and «Examinatio centri», each hyphenated «Exami-natio»; «Statio prima Veneris»; «Latitudo Veneris descendentis6)» over «prima» and «secunda» in smaller bold type. Here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L05-L09), the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. L10, the units, in bold.",
  "L11-L40. Checked as on p. 156 (JP2 0188): the Sublimatio is 2s 21° 15′ less half the Examinatio argumenti in every row, a half minute counted as a whole, to 2s 21° 15′, the apogee itself, at 180°, except at 178° (L38): there 2s 18° 25′ answers to an Examinatio argumenti of 5° 40′ or 5° 41′, where the edition prints 5° 37′ (note g) against the 17 of C and O; the note does not say «correxi». With 5° 40′ the steps of the column from 176° to 180° would be 156′, 162′, 167′ and 173′; with the edition's 5° 37′ they are 156′, 165′, 164′ and 173′.",
  "L11-L40, the Examinatio argumenti. The radius that reproduces each value as the equation of an epicycle is between 43.91 and 44.11 from 151° to 175° and rises to 44.56 at 179°; here a change of the radius by 0.1 changes the equation by up to 12′. The steps of the column grow from 24′ to 173′ a degree, irregularly at 155° and 165°, whose values, 42° 54′ and 33° 6′, stand about 4′ above the course of their neighbours, and between 172° and 173°, a step of 128′ between steps of 125′ and 143′. The Sublimatio follows these values.",
  "L11-L40, the Latitudo secunda. It is 5° · sin x to within 0.6″ in every row except at 168° (L28), where the degrees are printed 0: see the critical note. Its values for 180° − y are those of y on p. 156 (JP2 0188) except at 168°, 176° and 179°, where p. 156 has 1° 2′ 22″, 0° 20′ 57″ and 0° 5′ 16″ (0° 20′ 55.6″ and 0° 5′ 14.1″ computed, here 0° 20′ 56″ and 0° 5′ 14″), and those of Saturn on p. 143 (JP2 0175) except at 155°, 158°, 168° and 173°, where Saturn has 2° 6′ 46″, 1° 52′ 24″, 1° 2′ 22″ and 0° 36′ 33″.",
  "L11-L40, the other columns: the Examinatio centri for 180° − y is that of y on p. 156 (JP2 0188) in every row except at 159°, 0° 46′ against the 0° 47′ of 21°; it decreases by 1′ to 3′ a degree from 1° 4′ at 151° to 0 at 180°, and lies between 2.0′ below and 0.3′ above 2° 14′ · sin x. The Statio prima increases from 5s 18° 11′ at 151° to 5s 18° 21′ at 175°-180° by 0′ or 1′ a degree. The Latitudo prima decreases from 0° 41′ at 151° by 1′ a degree, with equal values at 158°-159° and 165°-166°, and from 167° on by 1′ every second or third degree, to 0° 22′ from 177° on.",
  "Notes on the readings. Note a: the last argument, 6s 0°, is N's; C and O have 5. Notes b, c, e and f are the edition's readings against C and O, without «correxi»: the Latitudo prima 0° 30′ at 163° (note b, against 34) continues its column; the Latitudo secunda 2° 11′ 31″ at 154° (note c, against 51), 0° 41′ 45″ at 172° (note e, against 42) and 2° 16′ 12″ at 153° (note f, against 52), 2° 11′ 30.7″, 0° 41′ 45.1″ and 2° 16′ 11.8″ computed. Checked: O's 1° 17′ 39″ at 165° (note d, against C's 27), 1° 17′ 38.7″ computed.",
  "L01, «Côaequatio»; L28, the degrees «0» of the Latitudo secunda: see the critical notes. L28: the second 2 of the seconds «22» is printed faintly. N05: the bracket after «17» of note d is printed without its upper arm; transcribed as «]». Italics: «om.». N01-N02: the ellipses «. . . .» of the lemmata as printed; N02-N03, «as-census», and N03-N04, «des-cendentis», divided at the end of the line with a hyphen."
 ],
